WEBVTT

00:10.744 --> 00:14.942
"Mudslide kills 600 religious pilgrims. "

00:15.582 --> 00:19.211
And yet both my ex-wives live on.

00:24.657 --> 00:26.522
Ahem. Morning.

00:27.026 --> 00:28.721
- Morning.
- Uh-oh.

00:29.696 --> 00:33.393
Tsk. Not again. Please, not again. Ugh.

00:33.566 --> 00:35.329
Thank God.

00:37.871 --> 00:39.736
Always in the last place you look, huh?

00:40.039 --> 00:41.506
Uh-huh.

00:41.775 --> 00:43.766
Have a nice day.

00:44.477 --> 00:45.739
You too.

00:49.415 --> 00:50.439
Phil, it's Charlie.

00:50.617 --> 00:52.585
Put me down for a grand
on Detroit tonight.

00:52.752 --> 00:55.744
What's the line now? Well, excuse me.

00:56.156 --> 01:00.957
But don't you think if the gambler is awake,
it behooves the bookie to be up as well?

01:01.594 --> 01:04.427
All right, well,
call me when you get off the can.

01:05.231 --> 01:08.132
Are you aware that your sleepover buddy
was packing heat?

01:08.301 --> 01:09.325
Oh, yeah.

01:09.502 --> 01:12.403
Any hotter
and she'd have burned my pubes clean off.

01:12.572 --> 01:14.699
Charlie, a gun in the house?

01:14.874 --> 01:18.310
Relax, she's a cop. Or was a cop.

01:18.478 --> 01:20.969
Or is wanted by the cops.

01:21.848 --> 01:24.112
I know she mentioned cops.

01:24.284 --> 01:27.048
Unbelievable.
So this was another one-night stand?

01:27.220 --> 01:30.314
Unless she comes back
for her handcuffs, yeah.

01:30.490 --> 01:33.926
Boy, how much satisfaction
can you get from that?

01:34.093 --> 01:36.323
Handcuffs? Not really my thing.

01:36.496 --> 01:38.088
But she probably did some stuff...

01:38.264 --> 01:40.824
...that might not have been
her first choice.

01:41.534 --> 01:44.264
No, I mean, how can you possibly
get any satisfaction...

01:44.437 --> 01:46.530
...from an endless series
of one-night stands?

01:46.706 --> 01:49.266
As the words come out,
I realize it's a stupid question.

01:49.442 --> 01:51.000
Forget I said it.

01:52.745 --> 01:54.610
She's married to a cop.

01:56.182 --> 01:57.945
I hate to see you wasting your life...

01:58.117 --> 02:00.677
...having drunken sex
with women you don't care about.

02:00.854 --> 02:03.789
Well, who asked you to move back in
and watch?

02:04.157 --> 02:06.625
- You know who was good for you?
- Don't go there, Alan.

02:06.793 --> 02:10.126
Mia. She was beautiful, she was smart,
she got you to clean up your act.

02:10.296 --> 02:13.732
I'm telling you, letting her go
was the stupidest thing you've ever done.

02:13.900 --> 02:15.231
You're going there, Alan.

02:15.401 --> 02:18.768
Just saying, you had this fantastic woman
who was willing to marry you...

02:18.938 --> 02:20.963
...and you just threw it away,
and for what?

02:21.140 --> 02:23.074
Okay, you're there.

02:24.844 --> 02:27.972
You wanna know why I gave up Mia?
I'll tell you why I gave up Mia.

02:28.147 --> 02:30.775
- I gave her up for you.
- Oh, for me?

02:30.950 --> 02:33.214
Yeah, yeah, for you.
She wanted you to move out...

02:33.386 --> 02:36.150
...so we'd have the house to ourselves,
but I said, "No way.

02:36.322 --> 02:38.517
I am not throwing my brother out
on the street. "

02:40.326 --> 02:41.657
Wow.

02:43.129 --> 02:45.996
- What a loving gesture.
- Oh, bite me.

02:47.667 --> 02:48.861
And you know what you did?

02:49.035 --> 02:50.832
You married Kandi
and moved out anyway.

02:51.004 --> 02:54.440
You wanna know why I let the best thing
that ever happened to me get away?

02:54.607 --> 02:58.509
So the worst thing that could ever happen
to me would have a place to live.

03:00.346 --> 03:01.904
Oh.

03:02.382 --> 03:03.940
"Oh. "

03:04.918 --> 03:08.376
Well, I guess it all worked out
for the best, huh?

03:08.554 --> 03:11.284
- How do you figure?
- Well, think about it.

03:11.457 --> 03:12.856
If Mia had been living here...

03:13.026 --> 03:15.119
...when Kandi kicked me out
and I came back, heh...

03:15.295 --> 03:17.229
...it would've been
a very awkward situation.

03:25.738 --> 03:28.070
Oh! Aah!

03:32.412 --> 03:35.210
Charlie?
- Huh?

03:36.482 --> 03:39.383
Oh, yeah. Awkward.

03:48.995 --> 03:53.932
Phil, Phil, Phil, you're my bookie,
not my psychiatrist.

03:54.100 --> 03:57.160
If I wanna bet every game in the country
with money I don't have...

03:57.337 --> 03:59.635
...that's my business.

04:01.607 --> 04:05.703
Thank you. Now let's talk boxing.

04:06.279 --> 04:10.113
Really?
There's no fights anywhere tonight?

04:10.283 --> 04:13.275
Okay, well, how are you
and your wife getting along?

04:14.587 --> 04:18.284
What? It would be a fair fight.
She's got like 50 pounds on you.

04:20.693 --> 04:22.251
Hello?

04:22.929 --> 04:27.457
My luck. I gotta have a bookie who's afraid
to fight out of his weight class.

04:28.101 --> 04:31.298
Arert you worried that this betting
might be turning into a problem?

04:31.471 --> 04:34.907
Alan, if you don't bet big,
you can't cover your losses.

04:35.074 --> 04:36.803
And if you can't cover your losses...

04:36.976 --> 04:40.070
...a large man with a tire iron
puts your address into MapQuest.

04:40.246 --> 04:42.339
You have to sneak
across the Mexican border...

04:42.515 --> 04:44.107
...dressed in womers clothing.

04:46.152 --> 04:50.521
- Now, that's when you have a problem.
- Well, you know best.

04:50.923 --> 04:53.448
You hungry? L...
I made your favorite sandwich.

04:53.626 --> 04:56.754
Turkey, ham and pastrami.
Heh, gooble.

05:00.800 --> 05:01.824
No, thanks.

05:02.001 --> 05:06.335
Okay, how about something sweet?
Key-lime pie. Yummy, yummy.

05:06.906 --> 05:09.841
Look, Alan,
I appreciate your sucking up...

05:10.009 --> 05:14.173
...but you can't fill the gaping wound
in my heart with deli meat.

05:15.948 --> 05:16.972
And pie.

05:18.985 --> 05:20.350
Yummy.

05:21.254 --> 05:22.881
Can't we just leave it alone?

05:23.056 --> 05:27.254
Can we not grind on and on
about the stupidest thing I've ever done?

05:27.427 --> 05:29.088
Okay, okay, I'm sorry I said that.

05:29.262 --> 05:32.698
Giving up Mia was not the stupidest thing
you've ever done.

05:32.865 --> 05:35.925
It wasrt as stupid as when you came back
from Rio with that model.

05:36.102 --> 05:39.299
You know, the one with the Adam's apple
and the really big hands.

05:42.241 --> 05:44.675
You know,
I'm gonna give you some space.

05:45.478 --> 05:47.844
Maybe go for a nice drive.

05:52.919 --> 05:54.614
Forgot my keys.

05:55.254 --> 05:57.017
Ahh... oh. Huh.

05:57.190 --> 05:59.590
You know,
they must have slipped out of my pocket...

05:59.759 --> 06:01.784
...and into the couch.

06:02.962 --> 06:04.827
Excuse me. Sorry.

06:09.035 --> 06:10.593
Sorry.

06:15.241 --> 06:19.541
Found some change. Ha-ha.
Oh, look, look.

06:20.346 --> 06:22.940
Is that a quarter in your ear?

06:30.656 --> 06:33.124
Ta-da.

06:35.661 --> 06:37.754
Very impressive.

06:47.940 --> 06:53.378
&lt;i>Aaah! Yeah!
Bab-em-stab-em-bab-em-bay-uh-dye&lt;/i>

06:53.546 --> 06:58.483
- What is that?
- Steven Tyler rented the house next door.

06:59.085 --> 07:02.282
The... The guy from Aerosmith?
I lost my virginity to him.

07:03.923 --> 07:05.481
Well, you know, his music.

07:06.359 --> 07:08.520
Thanks, I was confused.

07:12.565 --> 07:15.557
He's apparently getting ready for a tour.
So, what's...?

07:21.307 --> 07:22.865
- In the box?

07:23.042 --> 07:24.907
I went out
and picked you up something...

07:25.077 --> 07:27.739
...I thought might put a smile
on your face.

07:28.181 --> 07:29.808
Alan, the only thing in this box...

07:29.982 --> 07:32.212
...that could possibly put a smile
on my face...

07:32.385 --> 07:33.647
...is your severed head.

07:37.623 --> 07:39.284
Good one. Zing!

07:41.427 --> 07:42.451
Go on, open it.

07:48.034 --> 07:50.298
- A hat?
- A very expensive hat.

07:50.469 --> 07:52.164
Since when do I wear hats?

07:52.338 --> 07:55.466
Well, you don't,
but I saw it and it seemed so you.

07:55.641 --> 07:59.304
You know, cool, rakish, yet forgiving.

08:00.479 --> 08:03.880
- Okay, fine, I forgive you.
- Oh, thanks. Thanks.

08:05.418 --> 08:08.080
- Arert you gonna try it on?
- No.

08:09.622 --> 08:12.090
If you really forgave me, you'd try it on.

08:15.628 --> 08:17.994
Oh, yeah. That is you.

08:18.164 --> 08:22.032
Let's... Let's try tilting it a little bit here.
Oh, baby.

08:22.235 --> 08:25.830
Ha-ha. You gotta see this.
Come on inside. We'll take a look.

08:27.006 --> 08:28.701
Charlie, you coming?

08:35.348 --> 08:39.182
- What's going on?
- You should leave, Alan.

08:39.352 --> 08:42.014
- Why?
- Just trust me.

08:42.688 --> 08:44.212
All right.

09:04.877 --> 09:07.311
Hey, Tyler, take a pause for the cause.

09:07.480 --> 09:09.880
STEvEN:
Oh, sorry, man.

09:10.049 --> 09:13.212
Thank you and good night.

09:16.822 --> 09:19.222
- Hi, Charlie.
- Rose.

09:19.392 --> 09:22.725
How cool is it
that Steven Tyler moved in next door?

09:24.830 --> 09:26.889
I lost my virginity to him.

09:27.300 --> 09:29.962
- You mean his music.
- No.

09:32.371 --> 09:36.330
- Nice hat.
- Thanks. Boy, you look like hell.

09:36.509 --> 09:40.309
Well, that's strange,
because I feel like crap.

09:40.479 --> 09:42.913
How long do you think
you can keep it up?

09:45.584 --> 09:47.814
What exactly are we talking about?

09:47.987 --> 09:50.353
The excessive drinking,
the obsessive partying...

09:50.523 --> 09:51.956
...the compulsive gambling.

09:52.291 --> 09:53.349
Oh.

09:53.526 --> 09:56.791
Hard to say.
I try and take it one day at a time.

09:57.697 --> 10:01.599
You do realize this is all just an attempt
to avoid feeling your feelings.

10:01.767 --> 10:06.170
Let me tell you something about feelings.
Feelings are like your mother's breasts.

10:06.339 --> 10:09.934
You know where they are,
but they're best left unfelt.

10:10.109 --> 10:11.235
Interesting analogy.

10:11.410 --> 10:15.278
But may I point out that a mother's breasts
are a source of nourishment and comfort?

10:15.448 --> 10:18.315
Yeah, well, my mother's breasts
were a source of silicone...

10:18.484 --> 10:20.952
...and Russian vodka.

10:21.120 --> 10:24.851
Not good for child-rearing,
but she was a big hit at parties.

10:25.458 --> 10:28.359
Charlie, I know how much it hurt you
to give up Mia.

10:28.527 --> 10:32.793
And I know you don't like that feeling,
but the more you try to get rid of it...

10:32.965 --> 10:37.129
...the more it's going to come back.

10:38.637 --> 10:39.968
Oh, yeah.

10:40.139 --> 10:43.540
Perfect fit, like somebody measured
your head while you were asleep...

10:43.709 --> 10:46.473
...so when your brother called,
she could tell him the size.

10:54.720 --> 10:58.121
Hey, Uncle Charlie,
guess where I'm finally growing hair.

11:00.559 --> 11:02.390
Come on, man, I'm eating.

11:02.561 --> 11:05.325
Right here. I'm growing a 'stache.

11:07.066 --> 11:09.227
Oh, yeah, look at that.

11:10.503 --> 11:12.164
Hey, cool hat. Whose is it?

11:14.373 --> 11:16.341
Yours.

11:16.509 --> 11:19.945
- Really?
- Yeah. It looks great with the 'stache.

11:22.081 --> 11:24.606
It just occurred to me
that I've been feeling guilty...

11:24.784 --> 11:27.685
...because you called off your wedding
so I wouldn't move out.

11:27.853 --> 11:30.845
But then when I did move out,
you didn't call her.

11:31.023 --> 11:32.047
Yeah? So?

11:32.224 --> 11:34.215
So you know why
I think you didn't call her?

11:34.393 --> 11:38.022
You didn't call because the "I don't
wanna throw my brother out" business...

11:38.197 --> 11:40.757
...was a convenient excuse
to get out of the marriage.

11:40.933 --> 11:43.197
- That's what you think?
- Yes, that's what I think.

11:43.369 --> 11:45.360
That's what you think?
You heard me.

11:45.538 --> 11:49.497
- That's what I think.
Yeah, well, think again.

11:50.209 --> 11:54.703
Admit it, I've been beating myself up,
buying you pie and hats, for nothing.

11:55.281 --> 11:57.613
There's pie?

12:01.454 --> 12:04.981
There was. Berta ate it.
And why is he wearing your hat?

12:05.157 --> 12:08.558
- I gave it to him.
- I bought this hat for you.

12:08.727 --> 12:12.857
- And I gave it to Jake.
- You can't commit to anything, can you?

12:13.032 --> 12:15.694
- It's just a hat.
- It's not just a hat, it's a symbol.

12:15.868 --> 12:18.302
- Of what?
- Of...

12:18.471 --> 12:19.495
okay, it's just a hat.

12:19.672 --> 12:21.037
But the point is...

12:21.207 --> 12:24.608
...you have nobody to blame
for your miserable existence but yourself.

12:24.777 --> 12:26.574
Drink, gamble and hump all you want.

12:26.745 --> 12:28.736
One day
you're gonna have to face that fact.

12:28.914 --> 12:31.439
Drink, gamble and hump.

12:33.886 --> 12:36.787
Yeah, well, I don't have to face anything
I don't wanna face.

12:36.956 --> 12:39.390
And I don't have to feel anything
I don't wanna feel.

12:39.558 --> 12:41.355
That includes Mom's vodka knockers.

12:43.696 --> 12:46.927
Who is this vod Kanockers
that you speak of?

12:50.102 --> 12:51.194
Eat your dinner.

12:52.271 --> 12:57.140
The name's Kanockers, vod Kanockers.

13:12.558 --> 13:15.550
- Charlie?
- Shh.

13:15.728 --> 13:19.459
- You okay?
- Just dandy.

13:19.632 --> 13:22.465
Would you close the blinds?

13:22.635 --> 13:25.866
Come on. Let's get you inside.

13:26.038 --> 13:30.771
- It looks like you had a tough night.
- No, the night was great.

13:30.943 --> 13:33.741
It's the morning that's killing me.

13:35.481 --> 13:37.711
- Hey, Alan?
- What?

13:38.384 --> 13:40.045
You were right.

13:40.219 --> 13:42.744
I can't keep running away
from my feelings.

13:43.455 --> 13:46.891
- Well, I'm glad you realize that.
- You're a wonderful brother.

13:48.227 --> 13:51.321
And this is a beautiful hat.

13:54.600 --> 13:56.227
Thank you.

14:04.009 --> 14:07.001
- Charlie, are you okay?
I'm fine.

14:07.179 --> 14:09.647
The hat's not so good.

14:20.426 --> 14:22.587
Hey, Berta, wanna see my armpit hair?

14:24.196 --> 14:26.255
Only if you wanna see mine.

14:29.468 --> 14:31.561
- Hey.
- Hey.

14:34.440 --> 14:37.967
- You know that's my juice.
- I know.

14:38.143 --> 14:41.977
- You could at least ask.
- You could at least pay rent.

14:43.048 --> 14:44.948
Touché.

14:49.121 --> 14:52.386
If that's a bookie or a woman,
you know what to say.

14:52.558 --> 14:56.756
Harper residence. Sorry, he's dead.

14:58.063 --> 14:59.189
Interesting.

14:59.365 --> 15:02.027
No one ever calls back
to find out where to send flowers.

15:03.669 --> 15:05.660
Touché.

15:06.672 --> 15:10.130
How's it feel to go a whole week
without booze, broads or betting?

15:10.776 --> 15:12.767
It's actually kind of a relief.

15:12.945 --> 15:16.244
I never realized how much effort it took
to avoid feeling anything.

15:16.415 --> 15:21.375
- Yeah? What are you feeling now?
- So far, mostly nausea and boredom.

15:21.553 --> 15:23.987
Touché.

15:24.156 --> 15:27.648
- You don't know what that means, do you?
- Not a clue.

15:28.460 --> 15:31.725
Hey, if girls with big boobs
work at Hooters...

15:31.897 --> 15:34.229
...where do girls
with only one leg work at?

15:37.202 --> 15:39.432
IHoP.

15:48.681 --> 15:51.047
That's just cruel.

15:51.483 --> 15:53.747
Actually, it's kind of funny.

15:54.186 --> 15:57.553
Yeah, because they got one leg.
They have to hop.

15:57.723 --> 15:59.782
Right, IHoP.

16:01.527 --> 16:03.757
Tipping your waitress
takes on a whole new meaning.

16:07.232 --> 16:10.759
- It's not that funny.
- I know.

16:10.936 --> 16:15.771
- Then why are you laughing so much?
- I don't know.

16:16.375 --> 16:19.936
Dad, something's wrong
with Uncle Charlie.

16:20.112 --> 16:21.136
What's going on?

16:21.313 --> 16:26.478
Hey, Jake, tell your dad
how one-legged girls work at IHoP.

16:29.788 --> 16:32.552
Oh, no. I gave away the joke.

16:34.493 --> 16:36.654
I'm so sorry, Jake.

16:38.197 --> 16:40.688
I've ruined everything.

16:42.267 --> 16:43.598
Is he okay?

16:44.069 --> 16:46.560
He's fine.
His feelings are coming to the surface.

16:46.739 --> 16:48.639
Oh, like when Mom gets PMS.

16:50.509 --> 16:51.635
Well, kind of.

16:52.010 --> 16:55.502
Hang on, Uncle Charlie,
I'll get you some chocolate.

17:01.086 --> 17:04.749
- What's he making out there?
- A lanyard.

17:04.923 --> 17:06.515
He's got a lot of free time now...

17:06.692 --> 17:08.956
...so I gave him
one of Jake's old hobby kits.

17:09.128 --> 17:11.323
You know,
so he'd have something to do.

17:11.497 --> 17:16.594
I'm surprised he's not making a vagina
out of macaroni and bottle caps.

17:17.169 --> 17:20.263
Over, loop around...

17:20.439 --> 17:24.603
...around the block and then downtown.

17:30.616 --> 17:35.747
Over, over, loop around...

17:35.921 --> 17:38.685
...around the block and then...

17:38.857 --> 17:42.293
Yo, dude, some of us
are trying to do crafts here.

17:42.461 --> 17:46.454
STEvEN: What?
- Can you lay off the harmonica playing?

17:46.632 --> 17:50.033
STEvEN: Hey, a lot of people pay
to see me play harmonica.

17:50.202 --> 17:54.536
They pay to hear you sing.
They tolerate the harmonica.

17:54.706 --> 17:57.470
STEvEN: Sorry I don't measure up
to your musical standards...

17:57.643 --> 17:59.736
...you lame-ass jingle writer.

17:59.912 --> 18:02.312
Let's see how you play harmonica
out your other end.

18:02.481 --> 18:04.449
No, no, no, let's slow down here.
Come on.

18:04.616 --> 18:07.346
STEvEN:
Let's see what you got, jingle balls.

18:07.519 --> 18:10.283
I'm gonna rip off your big lips
and use them to kiss my ass.

18:10.455 --> 18:13.652
Charlie, please, you know your emotions
are a little bit frayed now.

18:13.826 --> 18:16.090
Right, right, okay. Okay.

18:17.496 --> 18:18.520
I'm better.

18:20.332 --> 18:21.663
- That's it.
- No, Charlie.

18:21.834 --> 18:24.064
Charlie, wait. Charlie, don't do this.

18:24.236 --> 18:26.534
Come on, Tyler. You want a piece of me?

18:29.575 --> 18:34.342
Well, the dude may look like a lady,
but you fight like a little girl.

18:36.348 --> 18:38.908
Did it ever occur to you to help me out?

18:39.084 --> 18:41.746
Yeah, but once you were cowering
under his picnic table...

18:41.920 --> 18:43.979
...I figured the worst was over.

18:44.156 --> 18:47.353
Though quick thinking,
squirting that bottle of sun block at him.

18:47.759 --> 18:50.751
I was hoping it would get in his eyes
and blind him.

18:50.929 --> 18:53.056
All you did
was keep him from getting a burn...

18:53.232 --> 18:55.393
...while he beat the crap out of you.

18:55.567 --> 18:57.865
Please, Alan, I'm begging you.

18:58.036 --> 19:00.664
Okay. It's not right to kick a man
when he's down.

19:00.839 --> 19:02.534
Thanks.

19:04.376 --> 19:07.345
Too bad Steven Tyler
didn't feel that way, huh? Heh.

19:11.783 --> 19:13.080
You were right about Mia.

19:14.553 --> 19:16.885
I got cold feet,
so I used you as an excuse...

19:17.055 --> 19:19.080
...to call off the wedding.

19:22.761 --> 19:26.857
I am so proud of you, Charlie.
This is a real breakthrough.

19:27.032 --> 19:30.559
And doesn't it feel liberating
to finally hear yourself admit the truth?

19:30.969 --> 19:33.335
Well, I feel something.

19:33.505 --> 19:35.905
But since I'm also
hearing a high-pitched whistle...

19:36.074 --> 19:37.905
...it might just be a concussion.

19:48.453 --> 19:52.651
- What are you making?
- A needlepoint sampler.

19:52.824 --> 19:56.055
- No kidding.
- I find it very calming.

19:56.228 --> 19:58.196
And the message helps center me.

19:59.665 --> 20:00.996
- "God bless vicodin"?
- Mm-hm.

20:02.401 --> 20:05.893
- Pretty good, huh?
- You spelled "vicodin" wrong.

20:09.641 --> 20:13.805
That's the great thing about vicodin.
I don't care.

20:15.580 --> 20:17.639
Hey, is Charlie here?

20:26.325 --> 20:28.885
Uh... Who may I say is calling?

20:30.829 --> 20:32.319
It's okay, Alan.

20:32.497 --> 20:35.557
- Hey, Chazz, thanks for the gift.
- You're welcome.

20:35.734 --> 20:38.430
- So no hard feelings?
- No. You?

20:38.870 --> 20:40.462
Why would I have hard feelings?

20:40.639 --> 20:44.006
I'm still picking pieces of your ass
out of my boot.

20:45.644 --> 20:46.668
Good one.

20:48.180 --> 20:52.378
- Okay, well, good luck with the tour.
- Thanks a lot, man.

20:52.551 --> 20:54.712
Who's the sponsor? Metamucil?

20:55.921 --> 20:58.719
- What was that?
- Nothing, nothing.

21:03.362 --> 21:06.195
I just wanna say I'm a huge fan.

21:06.365 --> 21:08.833
- I lost my virginity to you. Heh-heh.
- Really?

21:09.001 --> 21:12.061
Well, you know,
there's a lot of the '70s I don't remember.

21:21.847 --> 21:24.611
- Isn't that the hat I got you?
- Yeah.

21:24.783 --> 21:26.546
The hat you threw up in?

21:27.552 --> 21:31.818
I had it cleaned. But I'll always know.
